// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rules/global/ - the whole model. Copy this file, rename it, and delete this header.
//
//   Name it  <Topic>Rules.cs  and name the class the same: ConventionsRules.cs holds
//   ConventionsRules. Nothing binds the name to a table here, so name it after what it checks.
//
//   Rename to `.cs`. A `.template` file is not scanned, which is the only reason this one can sit
//   here without the run trying to execute it.
//
// When it runs   After the table rules, one file at a time in tier order.
//
// What you get   context.Tables  every table, so this is where rules across tables live - a
//                            reference in one table resolving into another, a convention over all
//                            of them. The static `Tables` reaches the same data globally.
//                context     IGlobalContext: reporting, and it still points at cells - pass the
//                            row and the field.
//                context.Schema, context.Option(...), context.Files(...), context.Json(...)
//
// Not here       context.Db(...) and context.Redis(...) - those are rules/runtime/ only, and not
//                on this type. No context.Table either: a global rule is about more than one, so
//                it names the tables it means.
//
// Priority       [RulePriority(-10)] on the class puts it in an earlier tier. Rules sharing a
//                value are one tier, lower runs first, and no attribute means the default tier 0.
//
//                It is a barrier rather than an ordering: if a tier reports, the tiers after it do
//                not run. That is what keeps a failed foundation from being buried under fifty
//                rules reporting its consequences. `tabbit --list-validators` prints the order.
//
// This folder is flat. A file one level down is not run at all; put shared helpers in
// rules/shared/.
//
// Full guide: doc/validation.md
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

